# Agentic Sports Slot Booking Bot — Python Rebuild

## Background

This is a complete rewrite of the [existing Node.js/Playwright/Prisma sports booking bot](https://github.com/Samay4405/sports-bot) that automates slot booking on the MIT-WPU sports portal (`sports.mitwpu.edu.in`). The original suffered from:

1. **Fragile hardcoded selectors** that broke whenever the portal's Next.js UI changed
2. **GitHub Actions cron delays** of 30–120 minutes, missing the 5:00 AM booking window
3. **Neon PostgreSQL cold starts** causing `PrismaClientInitializationError` crashes
4. **Silent failures** — the bot would fail without any notification to the operator

The rebuild moves everything to Python with an **LLM-driven booking agent** that reasons over live pages instead of using fixed selectors.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Oracle Cloud Free Tier Update (2026):** The Always Free ARM allocation has been reduced to **2 OCPUs / 12 GB RAM** (down from the original 4/24). This is still more than adequate for this project. Just note the limit when provisioning.

> [!WARNING]
> **Credential Migration:** Your existing credentials in the Neon PostgreSQL database are AES-256-GCM encrypted. We'll need your `ENCRYPTION_KEY` to migrate them to the new system. Alternatively, you can re-enter credentials through the new admin panel.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Dashboard Decision:** The plan uses **FastAPI + Jinja2/HTMX** for the admin panel (no React). This keeps the entire stack in Python and eliminates the need for a separate frontend build. If you'd prefer to keep React, let me know and I'll adjust.

